# CORVEX governance

Before writing or changing application code:

1. Read root `AGENTS.md` (Rules 1–6 + mandatory workflow).
2. Read `docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md` — stay inside approved capstone scope.
3. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — preserve as-built layout (`src/` + `backend/` + PostgreSQL).
4. Search existing implementations; reuse `src/utils/formatters.js`, `src/components/shared/`, `backend/lib/*`, and `ROLE_SETS` in `backend/middleware/auth.js`.
5. For schema work, complete `docs/MIGRATION_REVIEW.md` and run `npm run check:migrations`.

Do not invent requirements. Do not add out-of-scope modules (accounting, live GPS, extra roles, unapproved integrations). Do not delete lookalike code or run destructive migrations without explicit user authorization. Prefer small, necessary changes; report pre-existing debt separately from new issues.
